+# Contentful update timing
+
+The page loads `contentful-metrics.js`, which observes native Interaction
+Contentful Paint and Soft Navigation entries when the browser supports them.
+Durations are milliseconds from the initiating interaction to on-screen
+presentation, including asynchronous content updates. Each reported paint is a
+candidate update, not a finalized INP or LCP score.
+
+```js
+window.contentfulMetrics.support // { interaction: boolean, navigation: boolean }
+window.contentfulMetrics.getEntries() // most recent 200 measurements
+window.addEventListener('contentful-metric', ({ detail }) => {
+  console.log(detail.type, detail.duration, detail.interactionId);
+});
+```
+
+Records contain `type`, `startTime`, `presentationTime`, `duration`,
+`interactionId`, `navigationId`, and `url`. Soft navigation URLs are matched by
+interaction ID, including when paint precedes the URL change. An unmatched paint
+has a null URL; an earlier event payload can be enriched by matching a later
+soft-navigation event with the same interaction ID. `getEntries()` reflects
+these later URL associations. `clear()` clears local history and associations;
+`disconnect()` stops observation. Nothing is sent to a server.
+
+These APIs have limited browser availability. Unsupported browsers safely report
+no measurements; DOM mutations and animation frames are not substitutes for
+contentful presentation timing. See the [Chrome API documentation](https://developer.chrome.com/docs/web-platform/soft-navigations).
+
+The current site uses full-page links and has no client-side router. Soft
+navigation measurements will be emitted if client-side navigation is added and
+the browser detects an interaction, URL change, and visible content update.
+
+Run the observer unit tests without starting a server:
+
+```sh
+node --test tests/contentful-metrics.test.cjs
+```
